==Trivia==
* The [[Magnet]] Fruit has no description in the [[Blox Fruit Dealer]]'s shop.
** It has a large number of inconsistencies, pointing to an overall rushed release.
* While transformed, the mech suit makes a sound when the player sends a message in chat.
* The [[Magnet]] Fruit is the first fruit to have a disarm mechanic as part of one of its abilities, '''[F] Polarity Drive'''.
* [[Magnet]] is used by [[Awakened Bosses|awakened]] [[Cyborg (Boss)|Cyborg]].
* The [[Magnet]] Fruit was the first [[Natural]]-type Mythical fruit to be added without being reworked since [[Updates/17.1|Update 17.1]] in 2022.
* The [[Magnet]] Fruit is the fourth [[Natural]]-type fruit to have a transformation.
* Much like [[Kitsune]], Magnet is considered to be superior in base form, with the transformation only being useful for hyper situational/PvE settings.
* Currently, the Magnet fruit provides the highest damage reduction in the game (62.5%), higher than the [[Dragon]] fruit (60%).
* [[Magnet]] has one of the first [[Skins]] to fully change the transformation model, alongside [[Fiend|Runic Fiend]] and [[Empyrean]].
* The Stage 3 '''Flux Draw''' passive has a weaker magnetic pull and range in-game compared to its showcase in the update 30 trailer.
* Disarming an opponent with '''[F] Polarity Drive''' is just a minor issue for the opponent, as they can just equip their [[Swords|sword]] back instantly.
* Using magnet's '''[V] Maximum Overdrive''' while having [[Headband (Black)]] equipped, [[Shark]]'s V3 and V4 '''Leviathan's Armor''' passive active, highest [[Bounty and Honor System|Bounty/Honor]] defense buff (take damage from someone with below 500,000 bounty/honor), and [[Aura|Max Aura]] will grant the user 99.57% damage reduction, which is '''the highest defense possible''' by regular means.
* There is a current bug with '''Magnet''' which lets the user go through obstacles (some that can't even be passed with [[Flash Step]]) if the player holds {{Ability|F}} (transformation variant only) while being close to a wall.
* When transformed [[Power Meter|Magnetic Meter]] lasts approximately 1 minute and 56 seconds, without using any moves.
* Metal scraps last for around 30 seconds before despawning.
* There is currently another bug with '''Magnet''' that teleports players underneath the map when pressing '''[F] Polarity Drive.''' This notably happens in the [[Second Sea]].

